5 October 2026 - z80em86-88
---------------------------
Modified version of z80em86 1.0.2 (https://github.com/keusidan/z80em86-88).

Changes:
* Undocumented Z80 instructions (new file src/undoc.asm): IXH/IXL/IYH/IYL,
  SLL, DDCB/FDCB copy-to-register forms, DD/FD ignored before other opcodes,
  ED duplicates, other ED xx run as NOP.
* LD I,A keeps all 8 bits of I.
* R register counts opcode fetches (M1); bit 7 is kept from LD R,A.
* LDIR/LDDR/CPIR/CPDR with BC = 0 repeat 65536 times.
* Real time speed (new files src/timer.asm, src/timing.asm): T-states of
  every opcode are counted (Zilog UM0080 timings) and the PC timer runs at
  600 Hz to run the Z80 at 4 MHz. DOS environment Z80SPEED=4/8/0
  (4 MHz, 8 MHz, no limit).
* Z80 interrupts: EI/DI (IFF1/IFF2, EI delay), IM 0/1/2, HALT waits for an
  interrupt, RETN/RETI, interrupt acceptance in IM 0/1/2.
* The opcode fetch/dispatch code is shared (DispA-DispD) instead of being
  inlined in every handler, the code segment stays below 64K.
* 88 mode (new file src/pc88.asm): a program turns it on with OUT (0E0h),A,
  the warm boot turns it off. In 88 mode IN/OUT in the TPA access PC-8801
  style ports: 40h (BEEP, SING, VRTC status), E4h (interrupt level), E6h
  (interrupt mask), CLOCK 600 Hz and VRTC 60 Hz interrupts (IM 2 vector =
  level * 2), block I/O (INI..OTDR). Behaviour follows MAME.
* 88 mode GVRAM: ports 5Ch-5Fh put the blue/red/green plane (or main RAM)
  at C000h-FFFFh, port 31h bit 3 shows the 640 x 200 graphics in EGA mode
  0Eh (drawn at every VRTC), palette ports 54h-5Bh (digital and analog),
  plane mask port 53h. The 64K store is allocated before the RAM disk.

